#heading(level: 1, numbering: none)[Part II review]

You can now read any list-shaped data at sight. The load-bearing ideas: everything is an object built from cons cells (Ch 7); recursion follows the shape of the data (Ch 8); functions are values you can pass (Ch 9); sequences are lists with a standard vocabulary (Ch 10); and `loop` is the do-what-I-mean iteration (Ch 11). The project's alists — `*rooms*`, `*item-locations*` — were this part's running example.

If any of these feel shaky, the fix is REPL time, not re-reading: take one chapter's exercises and redo two of them from scratch.

